.TH INVOKE-AUTONOMOUS-MODEL-PHASE 1 "August 2026" "autonomous-run-governance" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
invoke-autonomous-model-phase \- run one fail-closed model-routed Spec Kit phase
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invoke-autonomous-model-phase.sh
-Action Validate|Run|Status -State PATH [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command resolves the strongest agent-neutral routing role declared by the
installed presets, binds it to one local runner profile, and starts preflight
and phase as direct executable-plus-argument-array processes. It never uses
shell evaluation and never silently falls back to another model.
.PP
DE: Modellwechsel erfolgen nur zwischen Phasenprozessen. Konkrete Modellnamen
bleiben in der lokalen Runner-Konfiguration und ausserhalb reproduzierbarer
Feature-Anforderungen.
.PP
EN: Model changes occur only between phase processes. Concrete model names stay
in local runner configuration and outside reproducible feature requirements.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -Action
Validate checks routing and profiles, Run executes one phase, and Status reports
the persisted routing state.
.TP
.B -State PATH
Feature-local autonomous-run-state.json.
.TP
.B -RunnerConfig PATH
Local JSON file with fail-closed agent and model profiles.
.TP
.B -RoutingRoot PATH
Installed preset directory containing model-routing.json files.
.TP
.B -PhaseId ID
Stable phase identifier required by Run.
.TP
.B -Prompt TEXT
Additional non-secret phase input.
.TP
.B -WhatIf
Print the resolved phase, profile, model, and effort without starting preflight
or the phase process.
.SH SAFETY
Missing routing, profile, executable, model, effort, or successful preflight
blocks execution. script-only commands are never started through a model
profile. Success grants no commit, push, merge, bypass, secret, deployment, or
provider-administration authority.
.SH SEE ALSO
validate-autonomous-run-state(1), orchestrate-parallel-autonomous-runs(1)
